    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d581-a2">

                <pb facs="0581" n="1315" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1315"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 657.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gargiulo to Mr. Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-29"><hi rendition="#italic">October 29,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report to you that this
                    evening I called on His Excellency Said Pasha, minister for foreign affairs, and
                    delivered him your note in which you requested him to inform me if he had
                    received your note, No. 93, of the 28th instant, and if he had replied to
                    it.</p>
                <p>Saïd Pasha acknowledges the receipt of that note, and says that as it referred to
                    two previous notes which were addressed to the grand vizier and the matter being
                    important he could not make a reply before finding out what steps the grand
                    vizier had taken on the subject, but anyhow, he said, you will receive his
                    answer by to-morrow.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. A. Gargiulo.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
